"""Convention followed: **Service pattern** — domain logic behind a
small class the provider binds for consumers to use. Controllers may
be wired separately and must not be assumed to call this service. Writes
use the unit of work; reads go straight through. Handlers that can fail on *expected* domain
outcomes (a row that is not there, a reference that is missing, a
unique collision) return ``Result[T, E]`` (Convention: **Result +
ProblemDetail**) instead of ``None``: the web layer's Result bridge
renders ``Err(NotFoundError)`` as 404, ``Err(ValidationError)`` as
422, and ``Err(ConflictError)`` as 409 RFC-9457 ``ProblemDetail``
documents. Infra faults (a dead connection) stay on the throw path —
they are not domain outcomes.

Application service for {{ resource_name }} backed by the SQL unit of work.
"""

